GeoConflux
==========

This product includes data from third parties. Their terms are recorded here, and the credit each
requires is carried on the dashboard where a reader will see it as well as in this file.


GeoNames
--------

src/Geopolitics.Infrastructure/Location/Data/global-places.tsv is derived from the GeoNames
geographical database, and holds every first- and second-order administrative unit on earth, the
settlement that is the seat of each, and the names those places carry in the languages that report
them.

    Source:  https://www.geonames.org
    Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
             https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Changes: Filtered to administrative units and administrative seats; alternate names restricted
             to the languages of each place's own country plus the languages this project's sources
             publish in; historic names, postcodes and identifier codes removed; coordinates rounded
             to four decimal places. Extracted by tools/gazetteer/global.py.

GeoNames provides the data "as is" without warranty or any representation of accuracy, timeliness or
completeness.

See docs/adr/032-global-gazetteer-sourcing.md for why this source was chosen.


Wikidata
--------

src/Geopolitics.Infrastructure/Location/Data/theatre-places.json is derived from Wikidata, and holds
settlement-level place names for the theatres under active tasking.

    Source:  https://www.wikidata.org
    Licence: CC0 1.0 Universal — no attribution obligation
             https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
    Changes: Filtered per theatre by bounding box and population; labels and aliases collected in the
             languages that theatre is reported in. Extracted by tools/gazetteer/extract.py.

Credited here because provenance is useful and because it is courteous, not because the licence
compels it. See docs/adr/026-gazetteer-sourcing.md.


